<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $25.9 mln June 13.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $25.9 mln June 13.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $25.9 million deficit on June 13 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JUNE 13</p>
<p>Exports: $197.9 million</p>
<p>Imports: $209.5 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $294.5 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $308.8 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $25.9 million</p>
<p>JUNE DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.233 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.604 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.764 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.475 billion</p>
<p>Net deficit: $82 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
